  "description": "Replacement of existing slate roof covering with Spanish natural slates to address repairs, prevent water ingress to the building fabric and weatherproof the building. Works include:\n\nRemoval and replacement of existing slate roof covering on front pitch and sections of the rear pitched roof facing the road\nInstallation of Spanish natural slates (500mm x 250mm) to match existing heritage appearance and surrounding areas\nReplacement of damaged hip and ridge tiles \nRepair of box valleys with new waterproof membrane and boarding\nRe-rendering of chimney stack and parapet walls\nInstallation of breathable membrane and treated timber battens using traditional methods\nAddition of vent slates to improve airflow for roof pitches\n\nAll materials selected to preserve the building's Victorian character and maintain visual compatibility within the Blackheath Conservation Area. \nNo change of use proposed. No alteration to building footprint or roof profile.",
